{
  "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUIRED",
  "findings": [
    {
      "class": "correctness",
      "location": "src/messaging/DeliveryRetryManager.ts, inbox claim acquisition; src/messaging/MessageRouter.ts, deliverSameAgentLocal",
      "finding": "A retry tick can claim a newly saved local `sent` message before its initial delivery starts. The initial router call sees the claim and returns. The tick rereads `sent`, has no executor for that phase, and releases the claim. The message can sit until TTL even with a healthy recipient. The initial-owner regression seeds `received` with `deliveryPending: true`, so it misses ordinary local sends. Reserve the initial claim before publishing the local record, or make the losing executor wait and recheck eligibility."
    },
    {
      "class": "correctness",
      "location": "src/messaging/MessageRouter.ts, deliverRelayed and deliverSameAgentLocal",
      "finding": "A delayed initial relay callback can bypass durable retry ownership. If the timer wins first and persists a busy result as pinned `queued`, the scheduled callback can subsequently acquire the released claim, reread `queued`, and immediately resolve and attempt delivery again. It consumes no retry reservation and can overwrite the existing pin for a legacy relay. Restrict the initial callback to its unarmed acceptance state under the claim. A regression should let the timer finish a busy attempt before releasing the initial callback and verify that the queued pin and retry budget remain intact."
    },
    {
      "class": "correctness",
      "location": "src/messaging/MessageRouter.ts, deliverSameAgentLocal TTL check",
      "finding": "The new TTL check subtracts the sender's `message.createdAt` from the receiver's `Date.now()`. A fresh strict message with a one-minute TTL can be accepted with a two-minute clock offset inside the five-minute signature window, then immediately fail as expired. Persist a receiver-local expiry derived from accepted signed age, remaining TTL and arrival time, and use it consistently in initial delivery and retry. The HTTP fixture explicitly uses one clock for both machines, so it cannot distinguish this case."
    },
    {
      "class": "correctness",
      "location": "src/messaging/MessageRouter.ts, currentSessionGeneration; src/server/machineRoutes.ts, MESSAGE_GENERATION_PATH",
      "finding": "An absent resolver returns `null`, which the endpoint signs as a completed no-holder observation. The sender consequently stops trying addresses and reports that the receiver has no unique running session. Return an unavailable response when resolution cannot run, reserving signed null for a completed lookup. This is distinct from the accepted loss of candidate and placement detail."
    },
    {
      "class": "observability",
      "location": "src/messaging/MessageDelivery.ts, final generation check; src/messaging/MessageRouter.ts and src/messaging/DeliveryRetryManager.ts, generation evidence",
      "finding": "A replacement detected after pin persistence or during the safety await correctly prevents injection, but returns `resolved-session-ended`. The router records `generation-changed` only for `target-session-generation-changed`, and the pinned retry terminal branch records only uncertainty. The rollout evidence therefore misses replacements at the final fence. Carry a distinct mismatch outcome through terminal persistence and assert the evidence event alongside the existing zero-injection assertion."
    }
  ],
  "resolved": [
    "The strict relay authenticates the domain-tagged wrapper before unwrapping. A path rewrite preserves a body the legacy handler cannot accept, and the envelope signature independently covers both generation fields.",
    "Strict acceptance uses `received`, `holderPending: true` and `deliveryPending: false` before pinning. The timer has an executor for that state and for the legacy unarmed `received` state.",
    "An expired admission waiter retires its map entry only after its predecessor chain settles. Broadcast machine `*` stays on its existing protocol, and caller-supplied generation fields are stripped at ingress.",
    "The final synchronous injection check uses the signed ID and rejects a conflicting mutable pin. The supplied cache regression exercises the production running-session lookup after synchronous cache invalidation.",
    "Physical send failure or exception retains uncertainty. Recovery handles armed uncertainty before TTL, final phase reporting reads committed state, and the watchdog skips confirmed pinned deliveries.",
    "The durable retry lane reserves work before acting, preserves cadence across restart and reports the actual retry count. Fewer opportunities under exponential backoff and reduced enabled-mode resolver detail are explicit tradeoffs.",
    "Inherited generic queued unpinned records remain outside the new lane. General notice durability and distinct-POST idempotency retain their separately assigned scope.",
    "Tests were reviewed as proof designs. No test execution or live rollout result is claimed."
  ]
}

{
  "verdict": "CHANGES_REQUIRED",
  "findings": [
    {
      "class": "CORRECTNESS",
      "location": "MessageRouter.deliverSameAgentLocal initialOnly guard and DeliveryRetryManager holderPending branch",
      "finding": "A delayed initial callback can bypass a durable retry reservation while the message is still waiting for a holder. If the timer wins newly accepted strict work, it persists holderRetryState, resolves a known role with no holder, and leaves the message received with holderPending=true. After the timer releases the claim, the initial callback accepts that same state and resolves again immediately. If the selected generation has become visible, the callback can type before the next eligible retry without charging an attempt. The queued-pin regression covers a different phase. Make received holder waits with an existing reservation exclusively retry-owned, and cover this ordering with the holder still absent on the timer’s first pass."
    },
    {
      "class": "CORRECTNESS",
      "location": "MessageDelivery.deliverToSession immediately before sendKeys",
      "finding": "Receiver-local TTL is checked before the awaited pin write and safety inspection. A message with little TTL remaining can pass that check, expire during either operation, and still reach sendKeys because the final boundary rechecks only generation. The active claim also prevents the sweep from settling it in that interval. Recheck the effective expiry immediately before injection and return a terminal pre-injection expiry result. A regression can advance the clock past expiresAt during the safety check while keeping the signed generation live, then assert zero sends."
    },
    {
      "class": "OBSERVABILITY",
      "location": "DeliveryRetryManager pinned retry branch at isPinnedSessionLive",
      "finding": "A bound message deferred by a busy session can encounter a replacement before its next retry. The early pin-liveness branch reports resolved-session-ended and exits before either executor records generation-changed evidence. The replacement receives no text, but the rollout evidence misses this prevented delivery. Distinguish an observed replacement from an absent holder and record the corresponding evidence after the terminal write. Exercise a busy deferral followed by a same-name replacement before the retry starts."
    }
  ],
  "resolved": [
    "The strict request authenticates the domain-tagged wrapper before unwrapping. Rewriting the path leaves the legacy handler with a wrapper it cannot consume, and stripping the wrapper changes the authenticated body. Strict sends disable redirects.",
    "Initially accepted strict work is downgrade-safe at received with holderPending=true and deliveryPending=false. A timer that wins initial ownership has an execution path under its claim. Expired peer-admission waiters retain their predecessor’s lane until the chain settles.",
    "Both recipient fields are signed as part of the complete message. The injection boundary checks the signed ID against the mutable pin and the current running session after the safety await. The supplied cache regression exercises synchronous saveSession invalidation through SessionManager.prototype.listRunningSessions.",
    "Arming persists received and typing evidence before injection. A failed final write leaves the committed phase visible. Recovery classifies armed uncertainty before TTL, physical false or throw is terminal, and the watchdog skips confirmed pinned deliveries.",
    "Receiver-local expiry accounts for accepted sender-measured age. Durable retry reservations preserve count and cadence across reconstruction. Fewer opportunities under increasing backoff are an explicit availability tradeoff.",
    "Loss of candidate names and moved-topic guidance during enabled preflight is an explicit frontloaded diagnostics tradeoff. Missing resolver returns 503. Legacy generic queued unpinned records remain inherited outside the new lane.",
    "Best-effort proactive notice durability and distinct POST idempotency retain their separately assigned scope. Tests were reviewed as proof designs only."
  ]
}

